  "content": {
    "id": "p18-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "Solve $12x^3-4x^2-3x+1=0$ if the sum of 2 of its roots is 0.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=\\frac13,\\ \\pm\\frac12$.",
      "worked": "Let the roots be $\\alpha,-\\alpha,\\beta$.\n\nSum of roots:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\alpha-\\alpha+\\beta&=\\frac13\\\\\\beta&=\\frac13\\end{align*}$$\nProduct of roots:\n$$\\begin{align*}-\\alpha^2\\beta&=-\\frac1{12}\\\\-\\alpha^2\\left(\\frac13\\right)&=-\\frac1{12}\\\\\\alpha^2&=\\frac14\\\\\\alpha&=\\pm\\frac12\\end{align*}$$\nHence $x=\\frac13,\\pm\\frac12$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 48
  },
